  "text_md": "## June 2014 21,\n\n## 25TH ANNIVERSARY POLISH AND EASTERN EUROPEAN GENEALOGY ROADSHOW\n\nPolish Genealogical Society of Massachusetts\n\n10 a.m. 4 p.m.\n\nPolish Center of Discovery Learning 33 South St. Chicopee; MA\n\nCome help PGS-MA celebrate our 25th Anniversary with a genealogy roadshow! For both beginners and experienced researchers, this will be a of fun and learning featuring four speakers, one-on-one consultations, and displays and help stations. S15 members/S20 nonmembers . day great\n\n## Topics Speakers\n\nUncover Your Roots in the Lemko Region of Southeast Poland Mike Buryk Beginning Your Genealogy Alan Doyle Horbal Naturalization &amp; Related Records Walter Hickey Poland What's That?? Stas Radosz\n\n## Displays &amp; Highlights\n\n- Free Scanning Station\n- Translation Stations (Polish, Russian; and more)\n- ~Ask a Genealogist' Tables\n- On-line Search Guidance\n- Find Your Ancestral Village\n- Polish Lunch by Bernats\n- One-on-One Session with Experts\n- Genealogy Raffle\n- Plenty of Chances to Meet &amp; Mingle!\n- LDS and Ancestry.com Stations\n\nThis program is supported in part by a grant from the Chicopee Cultural Council, a local agency which is supported by the Massachusetts Cultural Council, a state agency:\n\nFor more information, please visit http:llwww pgsma.org or call Ed Dzielenski, Board Member; 413-567-3132.\n\n## Thursdays June 26, 2014\n\n## TALK FOR REFUGEE WEEK\n\nPolish Refugees in Post-War Surrey: A Story of a Displaced Wartime Community by Wies Rogalski",
